(24,'HPV','Human Papillomavirus — the most common STI; high-risk strains cause cancer. Prevented by Gardasil 9.'),
(24,'Chlamydia','The most reported bacterial STI; mostly asymptomatic; curable with antibiotics; untreated causes infertility.'),
(24,'Gonorrhea','The second most common bacterial STI; drug resistance is a growing crisis.'),
(24,'Syphilis','Progresses through stages; congenital syphilis up 700% over the past decade; curable with penicillin.'),
(24,'HIV','Human Immunodeficiency Virus — attacks CD4+ T cells, progressively destroying the immune system.'),
(24,'AIDS','Acquired Immunodeficiency Syndrome — the final stage of HIV infection.'),
(24,'Antiretroviral therapy','The combination of medications that suppress HIV replication — allows near-normal lifespan.'),
(24,'U=U','Undetectable equals Untransmittable — people with HIV on effective ART cannot sexually transmit the virus.'),
(24,'PrEP','Pre-Exposure Prophylaxis — reduces HIV transmission risk from sex by ~99% when taken as prescribed.'),
(24,'Gardasil 9','The current HPV vaccine covering 9 strains — recommended for all people ages 9–26.'),
(25,'Noncommunicable disease','A disease that cannot be spread from person to person.'),
(25,'Cardiovascular disease','Any disease affecting the heart or blood vessels; the leading cause of death in the U.S.'),
(25,'Hypertension','Chronically elevated blood pressure (130/80 or above per 2017 AHA guidelines); the ''silent killer''.'),
(25,'Atherosclerosis','A disease in which fatty plaques accumulate on artery walls, narrowing and hardening them.'),
(25,'Stroke','An acute injury in which blood flow to part of the brain is interrupted — requires immediate 911 response.'),
(25,'Cancer','A disease characterized by the uncontrolled growth and spread of abnormal cells.'),
(25,'Tumor','An abnormal mass of tissue; may be benign (non-cancerous) or malignant (cancerous).'),
(25,'Metastasis','The spread of cancer from its original location to other parts of the body.'),
(25,'Remission','A period when cancer is undetectable or under control.'),
(25,'Diabetes','A chronic disease in which the body cannot properly regulate blood glucose.'),
(25,'Allergy','An immune system overreaction to a normally harmless substance (allergen).'),
(25,'Americans with Disabilities Act','The 1990 federal law prohibiting discrimination against people with disabilities.'),
(26,'Personal safety','The steps you take to reduce your risk of becoming a victim of crime.'),
(26,'Cyberbullying','The use of digital technology to harass, humiliate, or threaten — affects ~46% of teens.'),
(26,'Accident chain','The predictable sequence: unsafe situation → unsafe habit → unsafe action = accident.'),
(26,'Defensive driving','Driving with awareness of potential hazards and taking proactive action to avoid them.'),
(26,'Road rage','Responding to driving incidents with aggression or violence.'),
(26,'Graduated licensing','A staged system that increases driving privileges as new drivers build experience.'),
(26,'Personal flotation device','A life jacket or other approved device that keeps a person afloat — required for boating.'),
(26,'OSHA','The Occupational Safety and Health Administration — the federal agency responsible for workplace safety.'),
(26,'Fire safety','Practices to prevent and respond to fires — smoke alarms, extinguishers, and escape plans.'),
(26,'Distracted driving','Operating a vehicle while attention is diverted — texting is the most dangerous form.'),
(27,'First aid','The immediate, temporary care given to an ill or injured person until professional care arrives.'),
(27,'Good Samaritan laws','Statutes that protect individuals who provide reasonable emergency care in good faith.'),
(27,'Universal precautions','The practice of treating all blood and body fluids as potentially infectious.'),
(27,'CPR','Cardiopulmonary Resuscitation — emergency procedure combining chest compressions and rescue breathing.'),
(27,'Hands-Only CPR','Compression-only CPR — AHA-recommended for untrained bystanders responding to adult cardiac arrest.'),
(27,'AED','Automated External Defibrillator — delivers electric shock to restore normal heart rhythm.'),
(27,'Chain of survival','The sequence: Call 911 → CPR → AED → Advanced care → Post-arrest care.'),
(27,'Shock','A life-threatening condition in which circulation is inadequate to supply oxygen to body tissues.'),
(27,'Fracture','A break in a bone — requires immobilization and medical evaluation.'),
(27,'Concussion','A jarring brain injury caused by a blow or jolt to the head — always warrants medical evaluation.'),
(27,'P.R.I.C.E.','Protect, Rest, Ice, Compress, Elevate — the treatment protocol for sprains and strains.'),
(27,'Emergency survival kit','A collection of supplies needed to sustain a household for 72+ hours during or after an emergency.'),
(28,'Health care system','All the medical care available to a nation''s people, the way they receive care, and the way they pay for it.'),
(28,'Primary care physician','A medical doctor who provides physical checkups and general care.'),
(28,'Public health','A community''s effort to protect the health of all its people.'),
(28,'Health insurance','Private and government programs that pay for part or all of a person''s medical costs.'),
(28,'Air pollution','Contamination of the atmosphere by harmful substances including gases and particulate matter.'),
(28,'Smog','A form of air pollution created when sunlight reacts with vehicle and industrial emissions.'),
(28,'Radon','A colorless, odorless radioactive gas from soil — the second leading cause of lung cancer in the U.S.'),
(28,'EPA','The Environmental Protection Agency — the U.S. government agency responsible for environmental regulations.'),
(28,'Water pollution','Contamination of water supplies by industrial waste, agricultural runoff, or sewage.'),
(28,'Hazardous waste','Toxic, corrosive, or flammable materials that require special disposal to protect human health.'),
(28,'Specialists','Medical doctors who focus on particular kinds of patients or particular medical conditions.'),
(28,'Medical history','Complete and comprehensive information about your immunizations and any health problems you have had.')
